---
import Section from './Section.astro';
// The five evidence grades and the tone each is HELD to. Grades + calibration
// per CLAUDE.md, ENGINEERING_STANDARDS §4. HONESTY: the corpus today holds only
// Established + Probable notes — so only those two rungs carry a real note id;
// the lower three show the rule without pretending a note exists at that grade.
const grades = [
  {
    name: 'Established',
    tone: 'said plainly',
    eg: 'Higher fitness goes with a lower risk of dying early.',
    cite: '[exercise_mortality]',
  },
  {
    name: 'Probable',
    tone: 'lightly hedged',
    eg: 'Overnight heart-rate steadiness is a useful recovery signal, but a jumpy one — best read as a trend.',
    cite: '[recovery_readiness]',
  },
  {
    name: 'Emerging',
    tone: 'flagged as early',
    eg: 'Early evidence links overnight skin-temperature shifts to the start of an illness.',
    cite: null,
  },
  {
    name: 'Contested',
    tone: 'presented as debated',
    eg: 'Whether any single “sleep score” is truly meaningful is genuinely debated.',
    cite: null,
  },
  {
    name: 'Myth',
    tone: 'corrected gently',
    eg: '“You can train your body to need only five hours.” Not really — your sleep need is mostly fixed.',
    cite: null,
  },
];
---

<Section id="grades" labelledby="grades-h">
  <p class="eyebrow rise">Words matched to evidence</p>
  <h2 id="grades-h" class="rise mt-4 max-w-2xl text-[clamp(1.9rem,4vw,3rem)]">
    The wording matches the strength of the science.
  </h2>
  <p class="lede rise mt-6 max-w-2xl">
    Every research note carries a grade, and the grade decides how boldly it can be said. Overstate a
    shaky finding as settled fact, and the backing check stops it — exactly as a missing source would.
  </p>

  <div class="rise mt-10 max-w-3xl">
    {
      grades.map((g) => (
        <div class="grade-row">
          <div>
            <span class="grade-name">{g.name}</span>
            <span class="grade-tone">{g.tone}</span>
          </div>
          <p class="grade-eg">
            {g.eg}{' '}
            {g.cite ? (
              <span class="cite">{g.cite}</span>
            ) : (
              <span class="grade-none">— no note at this grade yet</span>
            )}
          </p>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </div>

  <p class="mono rise mt-6 max-w-2xl text-xs leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">
    Being honest about ourselves: the research library today holds Established and Probable notes only.
    The ladder still defines all five rungs, so the wording can never outrun the evidence — even for
    the weaker claims we don’t yet have a note for.
  </p>
</Section>
